---
// English Typing Guide & Layout Architecture Reference
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
---

<section class="mt-14 pt-10 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]">

    <!-- Section 1: Platform Overview -->
    <div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--accent-primary)]">
        <Icon name="lucide:globe" class="w-4 h-4" />
        <span>Typing Benchmark &amp; Certification</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-4 tracking-tight">
        Professional Typing Benchmark &amp; Skill Assessment
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        Touch typing is an essential skill for software development, administrative work, writing, and daily communication. <strong>TopNepali Typing</strong> benchmarks, analyzes, and certifies typing proficiency across four standard keyboard layouts: <strong>Nepali Unicode Traditional (MPP)</strong>, <strong>Nepali Unicode Romanized</strong>, <strong>Preeti (ASCII Typewriter)</strong>, and <strong>English US QWERTY</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The platform features millisecond-accurate keystroke latency tracking, grapheme-cluster-aware Devanagari character segmentation, lateral hand-load balance diagnostics, and verifiable certificates.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: Keyboard Layouts Architecture Matrix -->
    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">
        Nepali &amp; English Keyboard Layouts Comparison
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-5">
        Key distinctions in character encoding, physical key mapping, and application domains:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-xs text-left">
          <thead class="border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] text-[var(--text-muted)] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 pr-4">Dimension</th>
              <th class="py-3 pr-4">Nepali Unicode Traditional</th>
              <th class="py-3 pr-4">Nepali Unicode Romanized</th>
              <th class="py-3 pr-4">Preeti (ASCII)</th>
              <th class="py-3">English US QWERTY</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--border-subtle)]">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Encoding Protocol</td>
              <td class="py-3">UTF-8 Devanagari (U+0900–097F)</td>
              <td class="py-3">UTF-8 Devanagari (U+0900–097F)</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-amber-500 font-medium">Legacy ASCII Glyph Map</td>
              <td class="py-3">Standard ASCII / UTF-8 Latin</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Layout Topology</td>
              <td class="py-3">Remington Mechanical Standard (MPP)</td>
              <td class="py-3">Phonetic English Transliteration</td>
              <td class="py-3">Traditional Typewriter Keymap</td>
              <td class="py-3">Standard International QWERTY</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Web &amp; Search (SEO)</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-emerald-500 font-semibold">100% Searchable &amp; Accessible</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-emerald-500 font-semibold">100% Searchable &amp; Accessible</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-red-500 font-semibold">Non-searchable (Font reliant)</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-emerald-500 font-semibold">100% Searchable &amp; Accessible</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Target Key for 'क'</td>
              <td class="py-3 font-mono">Press key <kbd>s</kbd></td>
              <td class="py-3 font-mono">Press key <kbd>k</kbd></td>
              <td class="py-3 font-mono">Press key <kbd>s</kbd></td>
              <td class="py-3 font-mono">N/A (Latin k)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Primary Domain</td>
              <td class="py-3">Government, Banking, Publishing</td>
              <td class="py-3">Social Media, Chat, Software UI</td>
              <td class="py-3">Offset Printing, Archival Press</td>
              <td class="py-3">Global Business, Coding, Academic</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 3: Certification Benchmarks -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 font-bold text-sm mb-3">
          <Icon name="lucide:file-check" class="w-4 h-4" />
          <h3 class="font-display text-base text-[var(--text-primary)]">Certification Criteria</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs mb-3">
          To qualify for a Verifiable Certificate of Typing Proficiency, tests must meet both speed and accuracy criteria:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>Nepali Speed:</strong> Net speed must exceed <strong>20 WPM</strong> (&ge; 21 WPM) on Traditional, Romanized, or Preeti.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>English Speed:</strong> Net speed must exceed <strong>25 WPM</strong> (&ge; 26 WPM) on English US QWERTY.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>Accuracy Requirement:</strong> Accuracy must reach or exceed <strong>85.0%</strong>.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>Verification Record:</strong> Each certificate receives a unique ID, QR code, and permanent verification entry.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-amber-500 font-bold text-sm mb-3">
          <Icon name="lucide:award" class="w-4 h-4" />
          <h3 class="font-display text-base text-[var(--text-primary)]">Proficiency Tiers</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs mb-3">
          Candidates who surpass passing requirements earn classification ranks:
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-2 text-xs">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-2 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
            <span class="font-bold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Grandmaster (Speed Demon)</span>
            <span class="font-mono font-semibold">60+ WPM (NP) • 90+ WPM (EN)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-2 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
            <span class="font-bold text-cyan-500">Master Typist (Platinum)</span>
            <span class="font-mono font-semibold">50–59 WPM (NP) • 70–89 WPM (EN)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-2 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
            <span class="font-bold text-amber-500">Advanced Typist (Gold)</span>
            <span class="font-mono font-semibold">40–49 WPM (NP) • 55–69 WPM (EN)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-2 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-400">Professional Typist (Silver)</span>
            <span class="font-mono font-semibold">30–39 WPM (NP) • 40–54 WPM (EN)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-2 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
            <span class="font-bold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-500">Certified Typist (Bronze)</span>
            <span class="font-mono font-semibold">21–29 WPM (NP) • 26–39 WPM (EN)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 4: Speech Examination Mode -->
    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">
        United Nations General Assembly Speech Examination
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
        Standard typing tests often use random word sequences. TopNepali Typing includes an official examination featuring the historic UN General Assembly address by Kathmandu Mayor Balendra (Balen) Shah on Himalayan climate resilience and environmental responsibility. Available in full speech mode, 5-minute standard, and 10-minute endurance tests.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 5: Biomechanics & Keystroke Telemetry -->
    <div class="bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">
        Keystroke Biomechanics &amp; Telemetry
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm mb-4">
        Our analytics engine measures keystroke timing, physical layout scan codes, and corrective interventions:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-1">
            <Icon name="lucide:timer" class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-amber-500" />
            <span>Latency &amp; Hesitation Heatmap</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
            Tracks per-key latency to distinguish smooth muscle memory from cognitive pauses over 400ms.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-1">
            <Icon name="lucide:activity" class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-blue-500" />
            <span>Left vs. Right Hand Ergonomics</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
            Measures lateral keystroke distribution and error rates between hands to identify asymmetrical strain.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-[var(--bg-surface-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-1">
            <Icon name="lucide:zap" class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-purple-500" />
            <span>Error Recovery Cost</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
            Quantifies time lost to backspacing and corrections, demonstrating the impact of accuracy on speed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 6: Adaptive Drill Engine -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-500/10 via-[var(--bg-surface)] to-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-amber-500/20 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-amber-500 font-bold text-sm mb-2">
        <Icon name="lucide:zap" class="w-4 h-4" />
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-[var(--text-primary)]">Adaptive Weak Key Practice</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm mb-3">
        When you consistently miss specific characters—such as <code class="font-mono">o</code> and <code class="font-mono">w</code> in English, or conjuncts like <code class="font-mono">ध</code>, <code class="font-mono">भ</code>, or halanta <code class="font-mono">्</code> in Nepali—the adaptive engine automatically generates drills containing a high density of those target keys to build muscle memory quickly.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
